   <h2><span class="num">04</span>Respond.io — where leads go</h2>
   <p class="lede"><b>Takeaway:</b> unpaid enquiries book at 14.4% and paid enquiries at 1.5%. These figures are conversations and contacts, not conversions. WhatsApp Business API starts a new conversation when a person replies more than 24 hours later, so one contact can be counted more than once. The lifecycle status (New, Warm, Hot, Booked) is a separate field and does not reset with that count. We reviewed 12 months of Respond.io reports — the maximum available on the platform — together with nine months of lifecycle data. This covers 95,031 contacts and 73,069 conversations, managed by four human agents and one AI agent, with the AI agent currently handling 57% of assignments.</p>
+<div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><h3>Lead sources Vista reported, beside the Respond.io booking rates</h3>
+<p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary)">The booking rates above stay: paid 1.5%, unpaid 14.4%. Vista's Marketing Plan 2027 also reports where leads come from. The two are not the same denominator. Word of mouth 29%, Google 28%, others 8%, social, referrals, events and partners 5% each. That adds to 85%, so 15% is unaccounted. An alternative note in the same plan says Google 50% and walk-in plus word of mouth 30%. The denominator is validated before any target uses this split.</p></div>
